  "starterCode": "def pytorch_custom_dataclass(data: list, targets: list, idx: int) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Custom Dataset Class** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\ndef pytorch_custom_dataclass(data: list, targets: list, idx: int) -> dict:\n    if idx < 0 or idx >= len(data): return {}\n    return {'sample': data[idx], 'target': targets[idx], 'dataset_len': len(data)}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
